OpenBSD portable m4 licensing
=============================

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause AND ISC

The complete m4 executable is a combined work containing code under all three
licenses in the SPDX expression above.  That expression is suitable for the
package-level `licenseDeclared` and `licenseConcluded` fields of an SBOM.

File-level license map
----------------------

BSD-3-Clause:

  eval.c, extern.h, look.c, m4.1, main.c, mdef.h, misc.c, pathnames.h,
  stdd.h, tests/ack.m4, tests/hanoi.m4, tests/hash.m4, tests/sqroot.m4,
  tests/string.m4, tests/test.m4, and tests/ispc/**.

BSD-2-Clause:

  trace.c.

ISC:

  expr.c, gnum4.c, ohash.c, ohash.h, parser.y, reallocarray.c, strlcpy.c,
  strtonum.c, and tokenizer.l.

Portable-fork additions and repository support files without an embedded
license notice are distributed under the ISC license.  This includes the
compat/win32/** portability layer, CMake build and test support, and the
fork-specific GNU compatibility tests.  CMakeLists.txt is based on a script
released into the public domain; treating the resulting file as ISC-licensed
is conservative for redistribution and does not add another license to the
package expression.

Notices embedded in individual files remain authoritative.  The license texts
below are collected here to make source and binary license staging, compliance
review, and SBOM license verification possible using this single file.


